1
00:00:00,560 --> 00:00:02,000
- Why are you so eager for an answer?

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:03,560
- I want to finish it with you.

3
00:00:04,120 --> 00:00:05,160
- How about we meet tomorrow?

4
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:05,960
- See you.

5
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:08,400
- It’s just the two of us now.

6
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:09,560
- Let’s close the chat room, then.

7
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:11,080
- Wait, Mr. Bagel!

8
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,920
- Mr. Monsieur finally spoke.

9
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:15,320
- Let me swing by
my friend’s birthday party first.

10
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:16,320
- But we have plans!

11
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:17,600
- Stop f*cking bothering me.

12
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:19,280
- Go do whatever you want.

13
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:20,440
- Can you talk nicely?

14
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:21,840
- Cheers!

15
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:23,440
- I’m not getting serious with Dean.

16
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:24,240
- I know.

17
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:27,120
- Who would get serious with Dean
unless they were an idiot?

18
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:05,440
Here.

19
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:14,200
You drank so much you passed out.

20
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:19,960
Dean’s friends didn’t know
what to do with you.

21
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:22,240
They couldn’t get a hold of him.

22
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:28,120
That guy Hun realized you were my friend,
and he follows me on IG.

23
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:29,880
So I went there to pick you up.

24
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:35,920
I’m sorry… for bothering you.

25
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:37,640
It’s alright.

26
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:41,040
I’m your… friend.

27
00:02:50,079 --> 00:02:50,840
So…

28
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:53,840
Can you make it to your room by yourself?

29
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:58,600
Are you leaving now?

30
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:01,160
Can I stay over, then?

31
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:10,760
You never let me stay over,

32
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:14,960
and you don’t like
people going into your room.

33
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:22,360
To you, Dean’s the only exception.

34
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:29,240
Well, I—

35
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:30,360
You like him.

36
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:35,040
You truly like him.

37
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:38,400
No.

38
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:41,320
You even fell in love with him.

39
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:43,800
Tell me that’s not true.

40
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:47,640
It doesn’t matter.

41
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:53,920
It’s already over.

42
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:05,640
ONE WEEK LATER

43
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:10,320
But I still can’t picture
how this is going to turn out.

44
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:11,120
A little lost here.

45
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:12,680
Come on, Dean. At least try it for me.

46
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:16,959
It can be anything,
as long as my activity is on your channel.

47
00:04:16,959 --> 00:04:17,720
Wow.

48
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,000
Let me see.

49
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:21,440
You’re the perfect man for the job.

50
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:24,320
If not you, no one can do it.

51
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:37,840
Dean, I think I’d like to suggest this one.

52
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:39,480
What do you think?

53
00:04:41,520 --> 00:04:42,159
Do it for me.

54
00:04:42,159 --> 00:04:42,600
All right. Fine.

55
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:43,280
Let’s do this.

56
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:44,960
Let’s do this. I like this one.

57
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:45,480
Yeah.

58
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:46,480
Do it for me.

59
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:47,920
The layouts are actually pretty similar,

60
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:48,960
one and two.

61
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:51,920
One hot cappuccino, please.

62
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:53,600
We have a buy-one-get-one-free promotion.

63
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,040
Would you like to get two cups?

64
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:57,880
Uh, I’m just here by myself.

65
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,560
Can the other one be
a caramel macchiato, please?

66
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,760
Of course.

67
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:10,600
So, one hot cappuccino
and one caramel macchiato.

68
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:13,360
I’m using the promotion.

69
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:15,160
I’m paying.

70
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:21,880
All done.

71
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:23,320
All right, sir. Thank you.

72
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:35,640
You disappeared.

73
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:37,480
Who?

74
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:38,560
You.

75
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:41,080
You didn’t reply to my messages.

76
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:43,720
Who disappeared first?

77
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:47,200
Whoa. So it’s payback, huh?

78
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:51,440
No answer.

79
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:54,280
That means I’m right.

80
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:55,880
It means I’m not in the mood to argue.

81
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:01,200
Go back to your fling.

82
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:02,760
He’s not my fling.

83
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:03,560
He’s just someone I know.

84
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:05,480
He’s hosting an event,

85
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,880
so he asked me to make a review video.

86
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:11,720
It’s a blind-date event.

87
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:14,960
I’m still trying to figure out
how I’m going to review it.

88
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:18,880
Because you’ve hooked up with everyone?

89
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:24,320
Just kidding.

90
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:32,000
If you weren’t so cute,
I’d punch you in the mouth.

91
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,080
So what are you doing here?

92
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:39,400
I’m here to collect
my paycheck for the illustration.

93
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:41,400
The office is on the other side.

94
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:43,840
The one I dropped you off at the other day?

95
00:06:44,159 --> 00:06:44,760
Mm-hmm.

96
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:57,200
I…

97
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:03,360
I’m sorry I ghosted you that night.

98
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:06,080
I wasn’t in a good mood,

99
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:08,080
so I didn’t want to talk to anyone.

100
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:13,400
Mm.

101
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:15,040
And…

102
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:21,960
I’m sorry for saying those things to you.

103
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:26,040
You remember that?

104
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:28,080
Of course I remember.

105
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,160
I’m not a goldfish.

106
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:33,200
Is there…

107
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:36,800
anything else you want to apologize for?

108
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:41,240
Anything else?

109
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:44,520
What?

110
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,640
Never mind.

111
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:49,840
I’m leaving.

112
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,760
I need to deposit the check
before the bank closes.

113
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:59,080
[LET US MENTION YOU FOR A BIT.]

114
00:07:59,760 --> 00:08:01,520
You two met because
you dated the same guy.

115
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:02,440
Isn’t that weird?

116
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:04,320
It is weird, but…

117
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,320
we ended up liking each other anyway.

118
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:07,680
If you like someone, you like someone.

119
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:09,240
Why make things complicated?

120
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:09,680
Right?

121
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:12,360
Wow. You guys are adorable.

122
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,080
(If you like someone, you like someone.)

123
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:26,560
(Why make things complicated?)

124
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:31,800
Hey.

125
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,240
Will you reply to my messages?

126
00:08:38,799 --> 00:08:39,400
No.

127
00:08:43,159 --> 00:08:43,840
I don’t know.

128
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:58,640
(What makes people fall in love?)

129
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:01,480
(Looks?)

130
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:04,280
(Taste?)

131
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:07,120
(Scent?)

132
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:24,280
(Voice?)

133
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:27,640
Mr. Monsieur,
I never pegged you for a conversationalist.

134
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:29,480
If I didn’t get to talk to you one day,

135
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:30,400
I’d feel so lonely.

136
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:32,960
Mr. Bagel, have you eaten?

137
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:34,600
Is that a trick question?

138
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:41,240
(But that’s not as important as
the side of themselves…)

139
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:46,000
(they only let us see.)

140
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:49,200
I have something to confess.

141
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:53,160
If I’m…

142
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:57,080
not as good as I make myself out to be,

143
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:01,040
will you give me one more chance?

144
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:06,960
Hey.

145
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:09,120
Don’t laugh.

146
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:26,360
Let’s give it a try first.

147
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:29,200
Maybe…

148
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:32,800
my standards aren’t that high.

149
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:51,960
♪ One, I can’t hold back,
Just wanna get closer ♪

150
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:55,640
♪ Two, your name is all my heart whispers ♪

151
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:04,920
♪ Is it because I’m crazy,
Or because I’ve fallen for you truly? ♪

152
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:37,080
Pretending to sleep like last time?

153
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:45,880
Just get up already.

154
00:11:57,040 --> 00:11:57,880
You got work today?

155
00:11:58,600 --> 00:11:59,200
No.

156
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:03,040
Then you don’t have to rush out.

157
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:08,920
Another round?

158
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:10,560
No.

159
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:13,720
Just kidding.

160
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:17,560
Don’t you have work today?

161
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:19,440
I do.

162
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:21,920
Another review job.

163
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:23,800
Then get up.

164
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,320
Let me stay a little longer.

165
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:31,920
Five minutes.

166
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:33,120
Ten minutes.

167
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:36,800
Seven is enough.

168
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:04,880
Has it been seven minutes yet?

169
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:14,160
It has.

170
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:17,520
A little longer.

171
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:26,960
Hello, everyone. This is Everydeanlive.

172
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,480
Today, I’m taking you to try something new.

173
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:29,880
It’s a blind-date event.

174
00:13:29,880 --> 00:13:31,880
Every attendee
gets one of these scorecards.

175
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:34,320
Want to see what’s inside? Let me show you.

176
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:37,280
(Because the most important thing
in a relationship)

177
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:40,760
(isn’t what your eyes see,
but what your heart feels.)

178
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:45,760
(Yet, for the most part,
life is filled with rules and conditions)

179
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:47,280
(that keep our hearts from doing their job.)

180
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:48,880
Do you prefer mountains or beaches?

181
00:13:49,040 --> 00:13:50,080
That’s a tough one.

182
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,240
But I’d say beaches.

183
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:53,320
Where do you like to go?

184
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:54,560
I’ll be honest.

185
00:13:54,680 --> 00:13:56,040
I’m just here to review the event.

186
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:58,240
I’m not looking for a serious relationship.

187
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:00,600
Yeah, that’s right.

188
00:14:01,280 --> 00:14:03,280
This round’s for reviewers only.

189
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:04,480
I’ll get going, then.

190
00:14:06,520 --> 00:14:08,320
You secretly recorded
your conversation with someone else.

191
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:09,360
They’re going to chew you out.

192
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:10,640
Why?

193
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:12,680
I didn’t post it anywhere.

194
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:14,160
I only sent it to you.

195
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:15,480
Why?

196
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:18,760
In case you wanted to come.

197
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:19,760
Interested?

198
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:21,280
I’ve got a free ticket.

199
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:24,720
(The event owner said he wanted
some good-looking people to join.)

200
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:26,840
Ask the ones in your lineup.

201
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:28,560
Aren’t there plenty of them?

202
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:29,080
Whoa.

203
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:32,200
And here I am, asking the top pick.

204
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:41,160
(But at some point, some time,)

205
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:44,920
(with someone,)

206
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:47,600
(we have to let our hearts do their job.)

207
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:08,600
(We just have to find that point
and that someone.)

208
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:22,480
[GOING ANYWHERE TODAY?]

209
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:27,800
[THE GALLERY.]

210
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:44,160
[MOTH: WANNA GRAB A BITE?]

211
00:15:44,160 --> 00:15:47,560
[PUN: DON’T HAVE TIME.]

212
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:50,640
[PUN: I’M OPENING A NEW BRANCH,
SO I’M SWAMPED.]

213
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:32,960
Good?

214
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:37,560
So-so.

215
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:41,960
After four glasses of that, and it’s only so-so?

216
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:49,880
I’m thinking of taking bartending classes.

217
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:51,840
In case I ever want to open my own bar.

218
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:53,640
How does that sound?

219
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:55,400
Want to be my partner?

220
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:58,440
Partner up with you to open a bar?

221
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:00,400
It’ll go under.

222
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:05,880
Either you’ll drink everything yourself
or give it all away to cute people.

223
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:09,760
Dang. I thought I’d found someone
who’d go through thick and thin with me.

224
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:12,480
Go look somewhere else.

225
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:15,400
Because I’m not going through
thick and thin with anyone.

226
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:23,839
The dust hasn’t been as bad lately.

227
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:26,960
You can take your dogs out for a walk.

228
00:17:27,119 --> 00:17:29,400
But if you have a brachycephalic dog,

229
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:30,840
you need to be careful.

230
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:33,520
Hey!

231
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:39,880
I just went to grab the milk,

232
00:17:40,240 --> 00:17:42,000
and you ditched work
to listen to Dr. Pun again?

233
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:44,600
It’s rendering.

234
00:17:56,160 --> 00:17:56,480
Hey.

235
00:17:56,840 --> 00:17:57,560
What?

236
00:18:00,360 --> 00:18:01,960
You can’t keep living like this.

237
00:18:02,760 --> 00:18:04,320
I’ve got two choices for you.

238
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:10,040
One, tell Dr. Pun that the person
he’s been talking to online every day…

239
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:12,280
is you.

240
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:13,560
Why would I do that?

241
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:16,560
You know he doesn’t like the real me.

242
00:18:17,480 --> 00:18:19,480
If he finds out I’m the one
he’s been talking to on this app,

243
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:21,640
he’ll stop talking to me.

244
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:23,040
Fine.

245
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:25,480
Now for the second choice.

246
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:31,840
Get over Dr. Pun
and find someone else to like.

247
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:35,200
Someone you can talk to in real life.

248
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:40,400
Someone you don’t have to
talk to through this app.

249
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:41,800
Wait.

250
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:47,800
Damn it, dude. You know this isn’t working.

251
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:55,040
Today, Dr. Pun might go online
and talk to you because

252
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:59,080
he’s bored, desperate, or whatever.

253
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:03,400
But what if one day

254
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:06,840
he meets someone in real life?

255
00:19:08,040 --> 00:19:12,520
Do you really think he’ll keep
talking to you online for the rest of his life?

256
00:19:13,240 --> 00:19:14,520
Do you really think so, pal?

257
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:34,800
What do you want me to do?

258
00:19:37,080 --> 00:19:40,400
You know I don’t have any other choice
but Dr. Pun.

259
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:42,880
Give yourself a chance.

260
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:52,800
Hello, everyone. Welcome to Everdeanlive.

261
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:54,320
Today, I’m taking you
to do something a little weird.

262
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:57,280
Maybe it’s not weird to other people,
but it sure is to me.

263
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:58,720
It’s a blind-date event.

264
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:00,320
I’ve never been to one.

265
00:20:00,320 --> 00:20:01,800
You haven’t either, right?

266
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:03,320
Want to see what it looks like inside?

267
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:08,240
Dean.

268
00:20:10,240 --> 00:20:11,800
Will you go to this event with me?

269
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:13,720
Holy shit, dude! Are you serious?

270
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:25,960
What?

271
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:28,560
Can you ask Pun to come
to the blind-date event?

272
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:30,000
This Saturday.

273
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:31,240
I’ll give you the ticket.

274
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:31,720
Please.

275
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:33,440
Pun won’t go.

276
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:34,920
You haven’t even asked him.

277
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:38,080
Why?

278
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,880
Ran out of flings to mess with?

279
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:42,920
Now you’re messing with my friend?

280
00:20:46,560 --> 00:20:47,240
Want to know the truth?

281
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:50,080
You know my friend Ten likes Pun, right?

282
00:20:50,680 --> 00:20:52,760
Well… I kind of figured.

283
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:56,360
Yeah. Ten’s going to the blind date.

284
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:59,280
Who knows, the two might hit it off.

285
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:01,440
Pun’s not going to like Ten.

286
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:03,160
Why?

287
00:21:04,720 --> 00:21:07,880
Because Pun still likes you?

288
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:11,040
I can tell.

289
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,040
So what?

290
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:16,720
You’re being possessive of Pun
and don’t want my friend hitting on him?

291
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:18,720
I’m hanging up.

292
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:19,720
Hey, I’m joking.

293
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:20,960
Ask Pun for me.

294
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,400
Gosh, you’re ridiculous!

295
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:01,360
Hello.

296
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:04,360
Have you been avoiding me lately?

297
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,880
Why would I do that?

298
00:22:06,360 --> 00:22:06,960
Well…

299
00:22:08,280 --> 00:22:09,560
You’ve been kind of quiet.

300
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:12,720
I thought you might be mad at me
or something.

301
00:22:12,840 --> 00:22:13,920
Why would I be mad at you?

302
00:22:14,240 --> 00:22:15,720
I’ve just been busy with work.

303
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:20,120
And spending time with Dean
seems to keep you busy enough.

304
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:25,280
(Besides, people who just got together
should spend some quality time together.)

305
00:22:25,280 --> 00:22:26,040
Are you nuts?

306
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:28,600
I’m not serious about Dean.

307
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:31,080
Then what is it if you’re not serious?

308
00:22:34,640 --> 00:22:36,560
Things you never used to do,

309
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:39,120
you’re doing with Dean now.

310
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:41,480
That makes him special.

311
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:46,400
I just… want some romance.

312
00:22:47,040 --> 00:22:48,480
Someone to date.

313
00:23:07,640 --> 00:23:09,240
Come to a blind-date event with me.

314
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:10,920
Huh?

315
00:23:14,200 --> 00:23:17,600
Why do you want to go?

316
00:23:18,120 --> 00:23:20,480
Don’t you think
this kind of thing is nonsense?

317
00:23:20,920 --> 00:23:23,920
I just said I wanted some romance.

318
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:27,800
In case I meet someone interesting.

319
00:23:43,480 --> 00:23:44,120
Hello.

320
00:23:44,480 --> 00:23:45,000
Hi.

321
00:23:45,640 --> 00:23:46,640
I’ve already registered.

322
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:49,360
Okay, you have.

323
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:52,240
Here’s your scorecard.

324
00:23:52,280 --> 00:23:56,880
Inside are the pseudonyms
of the people attending the event.

325
00:23:57,120 --> 00:23:57,840
Sure.

326
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:02,280
[QUILLLESS HEDGEHOG.]

327
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:07,400
[ON MY WAY THERE.]

328
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:18,520
Hey, what’s up?

329
00:24:18,960 --> 00:24:19,640
(Hey, Dean.)

330
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:21,600
(Where are you? I’m at the event.)

331
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:23,560
What event?

332
00:24:24,040 --> 00:24:26,160
What? The blind date.

333
00:24:26,440 --> 00:24:27,600
(Damn, you actually went?)

334
00:24:28,120 --> 00:24:29,520
(What are you talking about?)

335
00:24:30,160 --> 00:24:31,040
(Where are you now?)

336
00:24:31,600 --> 00:24:33,000
I forgot. Sorry.

337
00:24:33,480 --> 00:24:34,560
But hey, it’s good that you went.

338
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:36,440
It might open your eyes.

339
00:24:36,720 --> 00:24:37,760
But Moth is here, too.

340
00:24:38,800 --> 00:24:39,080
What?!

341
00:24:49,120 --> 00:24:49,600
Hello.

342
00:24:49,720 --> 00:24:51,240
Why are you at the blind date?

343
00:24:51,320 --> 00:24:53,680
I asked you to ask Pun,
and you said it was ridiculous.

344
00:24:54,120 --> 00:24:55,000
I wanted to try it.

345
00:24:55,320 --> 00:24:56,120
(I even bought my own ticket.)

346
00:24:56,920 --> 00:24:58,840
(The one you gave me,
I already gave to Pun.)

347
00:24:59,280 --> 00:25:00,160
Pun’s going, too?

348
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:01,640
You asked me to ask him.

349
00:25:01,760 --> 00:25:03,240
But you said
you weren’t going in the first place.

350
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:04,480
You weren’t interested at all.

351
00:25:04,560 --> 00:25:06,160
Yeah? I never said that.

352
00:25:06,160 --> 00:25:06,680
You did.

353
00:25:06,880 --> 00:25:07,880
I said it was ridiculous.

354
00:25:08,560 --> 00:25:09,480
I never said I wasn’t coming.

355
00:25:09,640 --> 00:25:13,560
Hey. Stop saying one thing
and doing another.

356
00:25:13,560 --> 00:25:16,360
So, Pun’s going?

357
00:25:17,720 --> 00:25:18,600
He’s on his way.

358
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:19,360
Listen.

359
00:25:20,040 --> 00:25:22,320
Ten’s at the blind date, too.

360
00:25:23,800 --> 00:25:26,640
You can’t let those two meet
before the event starts.

361
00:25:27,120 --> 00:25:29,720
Otherwise, Ten will run off
before he even gets to meet anyone.

362
00:25:30,680 --> 00:25:32,080
Are you still playing Cupid?

363
00:25:32,160 --> 00:25:32,800
Please.

364
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:36,920
Whatever I say, please just go along with it.

365
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:39,960
Don’t let Ten meet Pun, no matter what.

366
00:25:47,320 --> 00:25:47,880
What?

367
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:49,560
I’m coming to the event.

368
00:25:49,720 --> 00:25:51,440
But can you grab me a coffee?

369
00:25:51,600 --> 00:25:53,800
There’s a café nearby. A few blocks away.

370
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:55,360
Go get it now. I’m sleepy.

371
00:25:55,360 --> 00:25:57,880
If you’re sleepy, don’t force yourself to come.

372
00:25:58,120 --> 00:26:01,360
Will you really have the guts
to join the event alone if I don’t come?

373
00:26:01,800 --> 00:26:04,040
Don’t you want me to help you
screen the candidates?

374
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:06,760
How long till you get here?

375
00:26:07,080 --> 00:26:08,280
(Not long. See you at the café.)

376
00:26:08,320 --> 00:26:09,280
(We’ll join the event together.)

377
00:26:15,080 --> 00:26:15,600
All right, guys.

378
00:26:15,600 --> 00:26:18,360
Please gather in the center here.

379
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:20,200
Right here, please.

380
00:26:22,680 --> 00:26:27,840
[YOU AND PUN CAN GO AHEAD
AND HEAD INSIDE.]

381
00:26:30,040 --> 00:26:30,880
Hello, everyone.

382
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:35,120
Welcome to “Blind Date Built to Last.”

383
00:26:36,240 --> 00:26:37,960
At today’s blind-date event,

384
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:42,040
you’ll receive a pseudonym sticker and
introduce yourself using your pseudonym.

385
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:45,200
This follows our concept:
“See their heart, not their face.”

386
00:26:45,240 --> 00:26:47,120
We’ll split you into Groups A and B.

387
00:26:47,120 --> 00:26:49,160
Each group will enter through
a different door.

388
00:26:49,160 --> 00:26:51,400
Inside, there will be a hut
where you’ll have your conversations.

389
00:26:51,480 --> 00:26:52,720
A partition will separate the two of you,

390
00:26:52,720 --> 00:26:55,240
so you won’t be able to
see each other’s faces while talking.

391
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:57,160
Each conversation will last five minutes.

392
00:26:57,520 --> 00:26:59,080
And don’t forget the rules.

393
00:26:59,280 --> 00:27:02,600
You may only introduce yourself
using your pseudonym.

394
00:27:02,680 --> 00:27:05,360
Your real name and contact information
will only be shared

395
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:07,240
after our staff matches your scores.

396
00:27:07,360 --> 00:27:09,400
Group A will enter through this door,

397
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:11,600
and Group B through this one.

398
00:27:11,840 --> 00:27:13,440
I hope you all enjoy the event.

399
00:27:13,440 --> 00:27:14,520
Thank you so much.

400
00:27:21,040 --> 00:27:21,520
Go ahead.

401
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:22,920
Just head inside.

402
00:27:22,920 --> 00:27:23,480
Hey!

403
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:24,360
Come here.

404
00:27:24,360 --> 00:27:25,880
I haven’t put my name tag on yet.

405
00:27:25,880 --> 00:27:26,560
You can do it inside.

406
00:27:26,920 --> 00:27:27,560
Go.

407
00:27:52,320 --> 00:27:54,560
(Everyone, please enter your hut.)

408
00:28:06,240 --> 00:28:07,600
I’m Surfing Dolphin.

409
00:28:11,560 --> 00:28:12,440
I’m Quillless Hedgehog.

410
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:20,560
There are almost a hundred people here,
and I just happened to meet you first.

411
00:28:22,920 --> 00:28:24,320
Why are you here, anyway?

412
00:28:24,760 --> 00:28:25,840
Why can’t I be here?

413
00:28:26,920 --> 00:28:30,320
Isn’t this event for single people?

414
00:28:32,520 --> 00:28:36,840
Haven’t you been single your whole life?

415
00:28:37,960 --> 00:28:40,960
In case I get lucky and find someone I like.

416
00:28:41,600 --> 00:28:43,120
Someone I can talk to for a long time.

417
00:28:46,840 --> 00:28:49,640
Isn’t five minutes too long?

418
00:28:51,040 --> 00:28:55,680
With you, two minutes is enough
for anyone to run out of things to say.

419
00:28:58,600 --> 00:29:00,200
I’m not as easy to read as you are.

420
00:29:00,880 --> 00:29:03,600
You open your mouth,
and people already know what you want.

421
00:29:03,640 --> 00:29:04,720
What?

422
00:29:05,560 --> 00:29:06,680
It’s called being friendly.

423
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:15,480
Once they talk to you, they’ll know
there’s no chance of sparks flying.

424
00:29:17,160 --> 00:29:17,720
Fine.

425
00:29:19,160 --> 00:29:22,640
I’ll show you how many matches I get.

426
00:29:23,320 --> 00:29:25,320
And if you don’t get any matches…

427
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:31,280
I’m not comforting you.

428
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:33,040
Who asks for your comfort?

429
00:29:33,840 --> 00:29:35,080
Maybe…

430
00:29:36,120 --> 00:29:38,360
I’ve already found
someone new to comfort me.

431
00:29:44,080 --> 00:29:45,320
You like to draw?

432
00:29:45,400 --> 00:29:48,080
If you ever need a model, let me know.

433
00:29:48,600 --> 00:29:51,000
Oh, I don’t draw portraits.

434
00:29:51,720 --> 00:29:55,080
I like taking portrait photos
at a studio in Phyathai.

435
00:29:55,360 --> 00:29:56,760
Then I hit a bar nearby in the evening.

436
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:59,440
You should recommend
some places in that area to me.

437
00:30:00,680 --> 00:30:04,080
Why give you recommendations
when I can take you there myself?

438
00:30:04,200 --> 00:30:05,600
What do you do in your free time?

439
00:30:05,600 --> 00:30:08,840
I edit videos. I don’t go out much.

440
00:30:09,040 --> 00:30:10,040
Do you like dogs?

441
00:30:10,040 --> 00:30:11,360
I don’t have any pets.

442
00:30:11,640 --> 00:30:13,600
I’m afraid I’ll get too attached
when we have to part.

443
00:30:13,680 --> 00:30:15,840
Hey, I’m allergic to pet hair.

444
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:17,680
We’re a great match.

445
00:30:18,120 --> 00:30:20,160
Well, I run an animal clinic.

446
00:30:29,360 --> 00:30:29,960
Hello.

447
00:30:31,800 --> 00:30:33,280
I’m Long Arm T-Rex.

448
00:30:35,360 --> 00:30:36,960
I’m Deep Water Capybara.

449
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:42,840
Hey, your voice sounds familiar.

450
00:30:43,680 --> 00:30:45,200
Are you…?

451
00:30:47,880 --> 00:30:49,200
I’m…

452
00:30:55,320 --> 00:30:56,640
Are you Mr. Monsieur?

453
00:30:59,320 --> 00:31:00,360
You’re here for the blind date, too?

454
00:31:02,960 --> 00:31:04,240
You recognize me?

455
00:31:04,800 --> 00:31:06,520
Of course I do. We talk every day.

456
00:31:07,040 --> 00:31:08,840
What about you? Do you recognize me?

457
00:31:09,760 --> 00:31:10,840
Absolutely.

458
00:31:11,640 --> 00:31:14,800
I just didn’t expect
you to come here, Mr. Bagel.

459
00:31:15,560 --> 00:31:18,800
I’ve been wanting to
try something new lately.

460
00:31:19,240 --> 00:31:23,720
My friend asked me to come,
and I was free, so I thought it might be fun.

461
00:31:27,800 --> 00:31:32,160
You wanted to try something new because…

462
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:39,040
you’re heartbroken over the friend you like?

463
00:31:42,440 --> 00:31:43,600
I guess you could say that.

464
00:31:44,640 --> 00:31:45,760
Happy birthday.

465
00:31:46,680 --> 00:31:47,320
Thank you.

466
00:31:49,600 --> 00:31:56,200
I used to think having a secret crush on him
was enough to make me happy.

467
00:31:57,360 --> 00:32:02,360
But things have changed.

468
00:32:03,680 --> 00:32:05,600
Do you really think
I’d be upset over something like this?

469
00:32:05,760 --> 00:32:07,480
Things you never used to do,

470
00:32:08,920 --> 00:32:10,040
you’re doing with Dean now.

471
00:32:10,640 --> 00:32:12,440
That makes him special.

472
00:32:13,320 --> 00:32:15,960
There’s no reason for me
to stay in the same place anymore.

473
00:32:16,320 --> 00:32:20,080
I hope you’re lucky in game
and lucky in love.

474
00:32:29,960 --> 00:32:34,320
It’s actually good timing for me
to try something new.

475
00:32:38,160 --> 00:32:41,160
You don’t sound heartbroken, Mr. Bagel.

476
00:32:42,200 --> 00:32:44,640
What a relief.

477
00:32:47,560 --> 00:32:49,120
If I’d been heartbroken over
a crush on a friend,

478
00:32:49,560 --> 00:32:51,720
I would’ve been dead from day one.

479
00:32:57,480 --> 00:33:03,200
My life right now feels like
I’ve just finished a difficult book.

480
00:33:07,080 --> 00:33:07,960
And now,

481
00:33:11,080 --> 00:33:14,200
I want to read something that heals my heart

482
00:33:16,320 --> 00:33:18,920
and makes me smile every day.

483
00:33:35,800 --> 00:33:39,080
Mr. Monsieur, what do you want from love?

484
00:33:45,040 --> 00:33:50,520
Um… I just want to
spend time with someone I like.

485
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:53,920
I’m not a complicated person.

486
00:33:54,400 --> 00:34:01,440
I want a happy relationship.

487
00:34:03,320 --> 00:34:04,640
Give them a ride here and there.

488
00:34:05,640 --> 00:34:08,280
Text each other when we’re lonely.

489
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:12,719
Whatever they like, I want to give it to them.

490
00:34:14,159 --> 00:34:15,800
I just want to live a joyful life.

491
00:34:17,320 --> 00:34:19,000
That sounds very peaceful.

492
00:34:20,400 --> 00:34:21,480
Life is really that simple.

493
00:34:36,480 --> 00:34:38,159
We have 30 seconds left.

494
00:34:38,840 --> 00:34:42,239
Is there anything
you want to tell me, Mr. Monsieur?

495
00:34:54,400 --> 00:34:55,320
There isn’t.

496
00:35:05,480 --> 00:35:09,280
As I said, everyone gets to meet everyone.

497
00:35:09,480 --> 00:35:13,080
For Round Two, we’ll split you
into Team Sun and Team Moon.

498
00:35:13,120 --> 00:35:16,760
You’ll get to talk to someone new
for five minutes, just like before.

499
00:35:16,920 --> 00:35:19,040
Get ready for Round Two.

500
00:35:19,120 --> 00:35:20,160
Please.

501
00:35:20,600 --> 00:35:21,560
See you.

502
00:35:22,360 --> 00:35:23,400
I’m going in now.

503
00:35:47,840 --> 00:35:49,280
Can I get your IG?

504
00:35:50,200 --> 00:35:50,800
Sure thing.

505
00:35:55,360 --> 00:35:55,960
Just followed you.

506
00:35:56,320 --> 00:35:56,920
DM me.

507
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:07,720
Is there anyone you like yet?

508
00:36:11,520 --> 00:36:12,080
A lot.

509
00:36:12,440 --> 00:36:13,040
Mm.

510
00:36:14,040 --> 00:36:15,400
Do people like you back?

511
00:36:17,560 --> 00:36:20,200
The event isn’t over yet. How would I know?

512
00:36:21,080 --> 00:36:21,960
But as for me,

513
00:36:22,120 --> 00:36:23,720
even though the event isn’t over,

514
00:36:24,840 --> 00:36:26,040
I already know the answer.

515
00:36:26,880 --> 00:36:29,000
(Everyone, please enter your hut.)

516
00:36:38,960 --> 00:36:40,280
I’m Surfing Dolphin.

517
00:36:41,400 --> 00:36:42,160
Are you Dean?

518
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:46,720
I’m Long Arm T-Rex.

519
00:36:47,080 --> 00:36:47,600
Hey.

520
00:36:48,680 --> 00:36:49,240
Ten?

521
00:36:49,640 --> 00:36:50,360
Moth?

522
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:53,280
How did you recognize my voice?

523
00:36:53,440 --> 00:36:54,880
Your voice is pretty distinctive.

524
00:36:55,920 --> 00:36:57,120
I recognized it after hearing it once.

525
00:37:00,400 --> 00:37:01,480
Pun’s here, too.

526
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:02,760
I saw.

527
00:37:03,760 --> 00:37:05,280
I managed to hide from him just in time.

528
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:11,280
Actually, you can just tell him you’re here.

529
00:37:12,040 --> 00:37:12,920
It wouldn’t hurt.

530
00:37:13,200 --> 00:37:15,160
Gosh. Yes, it would.

531
00:37:17,480 --> 00:37:21,760
But now that I think about it,
maybe it wouldn’t.

532
00:37:23,760 --> 00:37:25,520
He can’t even recognize my voice.

533
00:37:26,400 --> 00:37:28,560
Maybe you two don’t talk that much.

534
00:37:30,440 --> 00:37:33,120
If you did, I’m sure he’d recognize it.

535
00:37:39,600 --> 00:37:40,160
Moth.

536
00:37:41,880 --> 00:37:45,040
You’re the one Pun is closest to, right?

537
00:37:46,040 --> 00:37:46,600
Mm.

538
00:37:46,840 --> 00:37:48,600
Can I ask you something?

539
00:37:49,200 --> 00:37:57,160
Do you think there’s a chance
Pun could like someone like me?

540
00:38:00,080 --> 00:38:00,920
I don’t know.

541
00:38:02,160 --> 00:38:05,280
I’m just his friend. I can’t answer for him.

542
00:38:05,280 --> 00:38:07,360
Moth, you can be honest with me.

543
00:38:08,080 --> 00:38:10,120
You know Pun better than anyone.

544
00:38:11,840 --> 00:38:13,040
Why do you want to know?

545
00:38:14,880 --> 00:38:21,800
If I know there’s a chance
he might like me, I’ll go after him.

546
00:38:22,880 --> 00:38:29,800
But if there isn’t, I won’t do
anything that makes him uncomfortable.

547
00:38:29,920 --> 00:38:31,280
You can say it straight.

548
00:38:33,200 --> 00:38:34,800
Don’t worry about hurting my feelings.

549
00:38:35,560 --> 00:38:37,280
I can handle my own feelings.

550
00:38:43,400 --> 00:38:44,760
If I’m being honest,

551
00:38:48,760 --> 00:38:50,040
I don’t think Pun will like you.

552
00:39:08,200 --> 00:39:10,600
I didn’t think I’d
run into someone I know here.

553
00:39:11,360 --> 00:39:13,520
Well, I came with Moth.

554
00:39:16,120 --> 00:39:17,160
I’m sorry…

555
00:39:20,200 --> 00:39:21,600
about what happened
between Moth and me.

556
00:39:24,320 --> 00:39:25,800
It doesn’t hurt you, right?

557
00:39:26,400 --> 00:39:27,560
Why would it?

558
00:39:27,920 --> 00:39:30,640
You’re getting the wrong idea.

559
00:39:31,600 --> 00:39:34,240
Well, don’t you like Moth?

560
00:39:34,600 --> 00:39:38,640
I do, but I’m okay with it.

561
00:39:39,880 --> 00:39:41,520
You two can get together.

562
00:39:41,520 --> 00:39:42,640
No, no, no.

563
00:39:43,080 --> 00:39:44,280
Moth and I aren’t getting together.

564
00:39:46,400 --> 00:39:50,760
You two act like a couple.

565
00:39:51,480 --> 00:39:53,080
Isn’t that basically the same thing?

566
00:39:53,560 --> 00:39:55,800
Let’s just say, don’t think too far.

567
00:39:56,280 --> 00:39:58,440
Moth and I are definitely not getting together.

568
00:39:59,800 --> 00:40:01,320
Dean, listen.

569
00:40:03,200 --> 00:40:06,600
Neither you nor Moth is hurting me.

570
00:40:07,240 --> 00:40:08,440
I’m okay.

571
00:40:08,440 --> 00:40:11,600
Besides, I came here today to explore
and meet someone new.

572
00:40:12,960 --> 00:40:13,760
Mm.

573
00:40:15,520 --> 00:40:18,520
Hearing that makes me feel better.

574
00:40:20,280 --> 00:40:22,400
You don’t have to worry about me.

575
00:40:23,360 --> 00:40:26,360
I’m the one who’s worried.

576
00:40:27,440 --> 00:40:34,720
You don’t even realize how much
both of you are hurting each other.

577
00:40:46,200 --> 00:40:46,840
All right, guys.

578
00:40:46,840 --> 00:40:50,080
The search for someone you like is over.

579
00:40:50,080 --> 00:40:54,440
Now it’s time to rank
the pseudonyms of the people you like.

580
00:40:54,520 --> 00:40:56,680
Put the person you most
want to match with at number one,

581
00:40:57,000 --> 00:41:01,320
and the system will find your match
based on mutual rankings.

582
00:41:01,320 --> 00:41:04,520
The system will consider your preferences.

583
00:41:04,560 --> 00:41:07,160
If you both like each other
and rank each other highly,

584
00:41:07,200 --> 00:41:09,240
you’ll have a better chance of matching.

585
00:41:09,240 --> 00:41:13,880
Once you match, we’ll reveal
your match’s identity and contact information.

586
00:41:14,160 --> 00:41:14,800
Are we done?

587
00:41:22,920 --> 00:41:24,000
What am I even doing here?

588
00:41:25,960 --> 00:41:27,360
(I’m Long Arm T-Rex.)

589
00:41:27,920 --> 00:41:29,160
(Are you Mr. Monsieur?)

590
00:41:34,560 --> 00:41:35,720
[#1: LONG ARM T-REX]

591
00:41:43,840 --> 00:41:47,320
Are you sure you don’t want to rank anyone?

592
00:41:50,760 --> 00:41:52,160
[IF YOU DON’T CHOOSE ANYONE, OUR STAFF WILL ASK YOU A FEW…

593
00:41:52,160 --> 00:41:54,360
ADDITIONAL QUESTIONS TO COLLECT
FEEDBACK FOR FUTURE EVENTS.]

594
00:42:06,880 --> 00:42:07,960
I’m Quillless Hedgehog.

595
00:42:16,120 --> 00:42:22,160
[#1: QUILLLESS HEDGEHOG]

596
00:42:24,320 --> 00:42:29,920
You don’t even realize how much
both of you are hurting each other.

597
00:43:00,760 --> 00:43:01,800
What are you doing, Dean?

598
00:43:02,920 --> 00:43:04,160
Are you trying to match with everyone?

599
00:43:05,440 --> 00:43:05,920
Damn straight.

600
00:43:06,840 --> 00:43:07,280
Why?

601
00:43:07,880 --> 00:43:08,960
Everyone except you.

602
00:43:09,520 --> 00:43:12,000
Aren’t you going to rank Moth?

603
00:43:14,480 --> 00:43:15,240
Who said I wasn’t?

604
00:43:16,680 --> 00:43:19,040
I just believe in equality.

605
00:43:25,880 --> 00:43:27,840
[LONG ARM T-REX]

606
00:43:30,560 --> 00:43:35,640
If I choose Pun
but he doesn’t think I’m his match,

607
00:43:36,880 --> 00:43:38,160
I’ll be heartbroken.

608
00:43:38,160 --> 00:43:39,560
Maybe he thinks you are.

609
00:43:39,680 --> 00:43:44,800
But if he does, and we meet in person,
he’ll find out I’m Monsieur.

610
00:43:44,800 --> 00:43:45,680
Just write it down, man.

611
00:43:46,760 --> 00:43:49,760
If there’s a problem,
we’ll deal with it when we get there.

612
00:43:55,680 --> 00:43:57,880
[DEEP WATER CAPYBARA]

613
00:44:05,880 --> 00:44:06,480
Here’s some water.

614
00:44:06,560 --> 00:44:08,080
Wow, thank you so much.

615
00:44:08,120 --> 00:44:08,640
Are you tired?

616
00:44:09,040 --> 00:44:10,040
No. This is nothing.

617
00:44:10,160 --> 00:44:11,520
Your video really helped.

618
00:44:11,520 --> 00:44:14,160
The number of attendees keeps going up.

619
00:44:14,200 --> 00:44:15,280
- Thank you.
- No. Thank you.

620
00:44:15,520 --> 00:44:18,840
Oh, I’m gonna go help him over there.

621
00:44:19,240 --> 00:44:20,000
All right. Go ahead.

622
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:21,640
- Catch you later.
- See you.

623
00:44:37,280 --> 00:44:41,480
[QUILLLESS HEDGEHOG,
NUMBER OF MATCHES: 19]

624
00:44:44,280 --> 00:44:50,000
[SURFING DOLPHIN,
NUMBER OF MATCHES: 1]

625
00:45:16,960 --> 00:45:23,800
[GENTLE FOX]

626
00:45:40,440 --> 00:45:41,920
I can’t write down anyone else’s name.

627
00:45:42,400 --> 00:45:43,400
I only like Pun.

628
00:45:46,240 --> 00:45:47,960
You think I’m a total loser, huh?

629
00:45:51,440 --> 00:45:52,600
No, you’re not, dude.

630
00:45:53,880 --> 00:45:56,360
You came out today
and talked to so many people.

631
00:45:58,200 --> 00:45:59,200
But how did it turn out?

632
00:46:00,160 --> 00:46:01,440
In the end, you still like Pun.

633
00:46:05,960 --> 00:46:08,960
Right. It couldn’t be anyone else.

634
00:46:09,480 --> 00:46:10,680
He’s the only one I like.

635
00:46:26,200 --> 00:46:27,360
[SURFING DOLPHIN]

636
00:46:27,360 --> 00:46:32,120
♪ One, I can’t hold back,
Just wanna get closer ♪

637
00:46:32,160 --> 00:46:35,640
♪ Two, your name is all my heart whispers ♪

638
00:46:39,120 --> 00:46:45,040
♪ Is it because I’m crazy,
Or because I’ve fallen for you truly? ♪

639
00:46:50,320 --> 00:46:51,120
- What else could I do?

640
00:46:51,120 --> 00:46:52,480
- We matched,
so we have to stick together, right?

641
00:46:52,920 --> 00:46:55,160
- Thanks for taking pity on me.

642
00:46:59,800 --> 00:47:02,000
- Are you guys coming to the Good Boy Party?

643
00:47:03,080 --> 00:47:04,240
- What should I do, baby girl?

644
00:47:04,800 --> 00:47:05,920
- Just try.

645
00:47:05,920 --> 00:47:06,760
- Open your heart. Have you heard that before?

646
00:47:07,080 --> 00:47:08,440
- Hey, Dean!

647
00:47:08,720 --> 00:47:09,920
- Why didn’t you tell me you were coming home?

648
00:47:10,240 --> 00:47:11,840
- Didn’t want your boyfriend to meet me?
